      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name “Silverado” comes from the Spanish word for silver, “plata,” combined with the suffix “‑ado,” meaning a place characterized by that substance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/silverado-resort-186844",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Silverado Resort’s two championship golf courses were designed by renowned architect Robert Trent Jones Jr., cementing its status among golf’s elite venues.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/silverado-resort-186844",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nestled in the heart of Napa Valley, Silverado Resort is surrounded by rolling hills and lush vineyards that define the region’s landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/silverado-resort-186844",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area enjoys a Mediterranean climate, with warm, dry summers and mild, wet winters that make it a year‑round destination for outdoor lovers.",
